{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: ordinary evidence-only DESIGN review of jam-room revision 6 at exact b188c7f3d4509a6ff277498a22f947d627e3ac9a, tree 930c2e510cc8478908993c35317c99fdc13eb1c5. Primary e2e83c45 under invitation f9cdb29e / checker promise ce13a05b, as evidence for request 9ce8533f and builder promise 42eb0094. Apply the planner's already-issued decisions dff56797 to the note before adoption, so the artifact gives one settled scheduling and phrase model. This is a prose integration request, not a new implementation finding or a request for another spike/gate.\n\nThe note successfully replaces the old story with a person humming and an arriving band, makes the record/live boundary explicit, and attributes its numerical evidence carefully. No additional independent P1/P2 platform defect was established in this design review. The known conflicts now have owner decisions, but the current text still presents alternatives that those decisions exclude.\n\nRequired corrections, all from dff56797, which root read in full:\n1. Patterns have one DERIVED start bar. Remove the chosen-later-bar allowance at 932–936 and align the act table (182–186) and T5 (346–350). A pattern may name its length and interpretation; it never selects its start bar. Compute that bar from the entry time, historical lookahead and lower-sequence tempo schedule. Do not keep both the derived bar and a competing authored bar.\n2. Record sing.kind as tune or rhythm. The rhythm is a second sing; its interpretation changes tempo/grid and preserves the tune's key. Close the still-open question at 194–196 / 937–938 and carry the relation into the theme/interpretation descriptions. A percussion phrase must not silently replace the musical key.\n3. Put lookahead in the jam definition's rules ITEM, set at founding and changed by a rules act. The definition remains immutable; mutable application data can still change. Update the open home at 241–268 / 939–940, the fixed-definition-only claims at 393–397, R4 and the relevant P9 wording. Keep the historical configuration used by each pattern, including scheduled changes, so a later read does not use today's value for an old pattern.\n4. Close the recorded-refusal question: the caller receives the refusal and the stage shows it; no refused-act entry is written. The current substrate rule is already stated correctly. Distinguish the stage's display/capture from authoritative room history. A future durable refusal trace would be separately owned platform work.\n\nThese decisions are not yet text in the reviewed artifact. The planner's conditional adoption on approval is not an adoption act. Record the agreed model in the note and refile its exact successor; a prose-only revision needs no project test or gate rerun. The other five conflicts and nine platform gaps remain owned as dff56797 states, subject to Hugh's direction.\n\nCoverage: root freshly read the whole current note (56,378 bytes / 1,009 LF) and whole same-head plan 021 (8,008 bytes / 139 LF). An independent reader freshly read both and the complete native U3 (94,772 bytes / 1,613 LF), with 19 actual gap-free displays, at most 9000 characters and two slices per call. Root read the full report and ledger, independently verified all three native/capture/hash/count/gap identities, and read the original request's five conditions and planner assertion in full. Root personally read only the first 9000 characters of the U3; no root whole-delta claim or earlier-head credit is made. Seal /tmp/artroom-checker-jam-r6-b188-ordinary-root-binding.json, 9380 bytes, SHA256 22fc30a8b3d03e1fae2666fd8b692a7e0dcf5be6a9bc68efd70233e6acf5355d.\n\nArchitecture: the three clocks, sequence-ordered historical tempo/configuration and derived effect bars provide a clear deterministic record. Preserve those inputs across late arrival, tempo changes and lookahead changes; test live calculation against a fresh history read when implementation reaches that boundary. The live Worker carries copies, musical-time cues and clock estimates, while signed acts carry authority. The application stays in its own repository and uses published packages/service interfaces. No platform source import or application dependency is accepted. A local J2 harness establishes music and model behavior, not hosted grants or deployment.\n\nSecurity and usability: each player and the person sign their own acts; the stage authors no acts on their behalf. Instrument ownership guards and broad role grants are distinct; an instrument-scoped grant is not demonstrated. Member read sessions, renewal, watcher projection, browser key custody and live-channel authorization remain implementation work. Page transcription keeps the raw voice local under the proposed path; hosted audio needs its existing owner decision. An audio digest does not prove transcription accuracy. No private spike material or audio was opened or played, and no provider was contacted.\n\nEvidence limits and complete scope: J0 reports one tuned clip, Node CPU timings, tracker agreement and file-size counts. These are attributed producer/author results; they are not checker measurements, browser microphone/playback evidence, pitch ground truth or recognizability judgments. The original request still owes at least five real hummed phrases from two people, per-phrase timing/transcription and the singer's recognition judgment, plus the conditional audio-model comparison and recommendation. The private/uncommitted spike note was not independently verified. This note revision satisfies none of those completion criteria by itself.\n\nJ1 still needs the actual deployed version, sample counts, p50/p99, retries and cold/warm state. J2 still needs real model-call time/cost, a second theme and a human musical judgment. Clarify its 95% before-start-bar metric: delivery before an effect bar derived after commit does not alone show timely generation or a funny stop-to-downbeat response. Keep an intended phrase deadline or report the actual interval alongside the existing target and human judgment. This is a nonblocking measurement clarification, not a proved timing failure.\n\nSimplification and scalability: one pattern act avoids bringing the file/push/checker pipeline into the first phrase. The new story may set aside its earlier sample/MIDI path as explicitly dated application scope; it waives no complete Artroom functionality. Thirty or 120 pattern entries per minute exclude theme, interpretation, arrival, solo, banter and release overhead. The rough 55/14-hour figures are ceilings from one temporary entry budget, not indefinite-session or whole-capacity acceptance. Keep rollover/continuity, all five dimensions, throughput and retention duties with their owners.\n\nThe note's main 48a2 baseline is explicitly dated. M3 is now landed and published as f47fc598, which improves register/directory founding but still stops at the destination; this does not make the historical baseline false or prove a hosted jam. Use a dated update when reconciling current source. Preserve package publication, complete founding, deployment, application key/live interfaces, meaningful agent permissions, mutable rules and session continuity as owned work. No live service, human/audio result, provider, browser, capacity or source acceptance follows.\n\nValidation used immutable native Git, builtin static text/hash/count, /tmp evidence and normal gitseq only. No project imports/execution/tests/gate/build/install/typecheck/evaluator/simulation/generated histories/private diagnostics/provider/contact/process/source edits/merge/push; forbidden cloud-review/static-ledger bodies were never opened. Final prepare confirms evidence-only for 9ce8533f, the sole primary artifact and no implementations supplied. No request/J0/I3/full-application closure or design adoption is declared.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e2e83c451f4a3d5d9c229f9c70bdbeaaf7cbfe14","binding":"evidence-only","head":"b188c7f3d4509a6ff277498a22f947d627e3ac9a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ce13a05bd6c59711c70503c8e064dbc4a1786325\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e37ef560b61720f00489faef0ed70396f03174d7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}